  "id": "Compound::DB00855 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Aminolevulinic Acid appears to interact with Slc15a1 through binding, which is a common mechanism in drug-target interactions. This binding leads to Slc15a1 participating in various transport activities, including proton-dependent peptide transport and proton/oligonucleotide cotransport. These activities are all part of a broader functional category that Slc15a2 participates in, suggesting a potential functional overlap between Slc15a1 and Slc15a2. The evidence suggests that Aminolevulinic Acid may influence Slc15a2 through a shared pathway involving Slc15a1, which could be critical for understanding the role of these proteins in cellular transport processes. The consistent binding and participation patterns across the three paths indicate a plausible mechanism by which Aminolevulinic Acid might affect Slc15a2, though further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
